# default gitignore spring initializr generates for every new maven project, mostly untouched

# help.md is the getting started file initializr drops in, not something worth keeping in git
HELP.md
# maven build output, target/ is where all the compiled classes and the packaged jar end up
target/
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
# these two exist in case a source folder literally has a subfolder named target, an edge case
# initializr guards against by default, does not really come up in this project
!**/src/main/**/target/
!**/src/test/**/target/

### STS ###
# spring tool suite specific files, not the ide I actually use but initializr includes this by default
.apt_generated
.classpath
.factorypath
.project
.settings
.springBeans
.sts4-cache

### IntelliJ IDEA ###
# this is the one that actually matters here since intellij is what I built this with
.idea
*.iws
*.iml
*.ipr

### NetBeans ###
# not used on this project either, just part of the standard initializr template
/nbproject/private/
/nbbuild/
/dist/
/nbdist/
/.nb-gradle/
build/
!**/src/main/**/build/
!**/src/test/**/build/

### VS Code ###
# same idea as the root gitignore, keeping this per module copy since initializr generates it that way
.vscode/
